)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@TUTORIAL: Using the Tutorial                   !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                  }
}
}  The tutorial is a row of panels. Each part leads to the next one, so
}  you can go through the whole course with the Enter key alone.
}
{    Enter            }the next panel
{    Left key, PF10   }the panel before
{    Up key, PF7      }the tutorial's list of parts
{    End key, PF3     }leave the tutorial, back to the SDSF panel
{    T                }the table of contents of the help
}
}  Some panels show an SDSF panel as an example and ask you to type
}  something on it, as you would on the real one. The tutorial answers as
}  SDSF would; nothing is done to any job.
}
}  SDSF commands such as ST are not taken on tutorial panels. To try one
}  for real, leave the tutorial with the End key, then start it again
}  with TUTOR when you like.
}
}
}  Enter: part 2   PF7: list of parts   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFTPAN
  &ZUP = ISFTUTOR
)END
